# License

**Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported
(CC BY-NC-SA 3.0)**

- Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/
- Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/legalcode

## Why this license

This firmware descends from **Qlockthree** by Christian Aschoff. His download
page states, next to the firmware itself:

> "Die Programme unterliegen der CC BY-NC-SA 3.0-Lizenz (Namensnennung -
> Nicht-kommerziell - Weitergabe unter gleichen Bedingungen 3.0)."
>
> — http://www.christians-bastel-laden.de/DOWNLOADS/index.html

The ShareAlike term requires derivative works to be distributed under the same
or a comparable license, so this is inherited rather than chosen. Files that
still carry his authorship say so in their headers.

## What it means in practice

- **Attribution** — keep the author lines in the file headers, and name the
  origin when you pass the work on.
- **NonCommercial** — no commercial use. Selling clocks or kits running this
  firmware is not covered.
- **ShareAlike** — anything you build on it goes out under these same terms.

Note that CC BY-NC-SA is not an OSI-approved open source license, and Creative
Commons themselves advise against using CC licenses for software. It applies
here because the upstream work does, not because it is a good fit for code.

